# ✅ 1. **width()** – sets minimum width of output

```cpp
#include <iostream>
using namespace std;

int main() {
    cout << "Normal: " << 123 << endl;

    cout << "Width(10): ";
    cout.width(10);       // reserve 10 spaces
    cout << 123 << endl;  // number appears right-aligned

    return 0;
}
```

**Output:**

```
Normal: 123
Width(10):        123
```

