# ⭐ 3. Accessing Class Members

Private data CAN'T be accessed directly.

WRONG:
```cpp
x.number = 10; // error (private)
```

You MUST use member functions.

---

## ✔ How to call member functions

### Format from screenshot:
```
object-name.function-name(arguments);
```

### Example:
```cpp
x.getdata(100, 75.5);
x.putdata();
```

---

# ⭐ FULL CODE for Accessing Members

```cpp
#include <iostream>
using namespace std;

class item {
private:
    int number;
    float cost;

public:
    void getdata(int a, float b) {
        number = a;
        cost = b;
    }

    void putdata() {
        cout << "Number = " << number << endl;
        cout << "Cost   = " << cost << endl;
    }
};

int main() {
    item x;

    x.getdata(100, 75.5);  // sets values
    x.putdata();           // prints values

    return 0;
}
```

### Output
```
Number = 100
Cost   = 75.5
```

