• Different classes may have functions with identical names; scope resolution resolves them.
• Member functions may call other member functions directly.
• Member functions may be defined inside or outside a class.
• Functions defined inside a class are treated as inline.
• Outside functions can be made inline using the inline keyword.
• Inline functions improve speed by eliminating function call overhead.
```

